  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1247 PM MDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nA weak disturbance spinning up into the Southwest this afternoon\nwill send some cloud cover across the region late this evening\nand Sunday. This will aid the cool trend in temperatures\ncontinuing Sunday and Monday. While moisture looks anemic with\nthis wave, it does look like we manage to get some light rain\ninto southeast UT and southwest CO Sunday afternoon and evening.\nFreezing levels remain high enough to isolate snow to above\ntreeline in the San Juans, where very little snow is expected\nanyway. Weak shortwave perturbations continue to ripple across\nthe southern half of the CWA on Monday and Tuesday, ahead of a\ndeeper more organized system coming ashore out west. Stronger\nsouthwest flow will return temperatures to the normal range\nTuesday and Wednesday.\n\nEarly Wednesday, a deeper pool of moisture lifts into the Four\nCorners ahead of the previously mentioned system. This is\nexpected to produce more substantial rainfall for southern CO\nand southeast UT. This could also produce some additional\nsnowfall for the mountains, depending on depth of cold air on\nthe backside of this system. Cooler temperatures return Friday\nand Saturday as cold air pools in the region, while unsettled\nconditions continue for the mountains.",
